<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of People's Commissars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sovnarkom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of People's Commissars, or Sovnarkom, was the government of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, formed by the Second Congress of Soviets during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> of 1917 with Lenin as chairman. Its members, the people's commissars, headed the government <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a>. A Sovnarkom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was created in 1923, and in 1946 the councils were renamed councils of ministers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-peoples-commissars.jpg" alt="Council of People's Commissars" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Совнарком 1919 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1919-SovNarkom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
